          "quote": "(node (ref \"R18\") (pin \"1\"))(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"A\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two mutually-exclusive servo interface modes, selected at assembly time by populating different 0 Ω jumper resistors"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "PWM mode ... each servo header's signal pin gets its own independent ... GPIO line"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The servo signal pins are not independent, and the serial transceiver path is connected at the same time as the GPIO signal paths. This can cause signal contention or prevent correct operation in the intended PWM or serial configuration.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["R7", "R15", "R17", "R24"],
      "pins": ["J5.19", "J5.21", "J5.20", "J5.22"],
      "nets": ["/NET0013", "/NET0023", "/NET0011", "/NET0042", "/NET0040", "/NET0044"],
      "observed": "All four links are 0 Ω. R7 and R15 connect M-BUS pins 19 and 21 through /NET0040; R17 and R24 connect pins 20 and 22 through /NET0044.",
      "expected": "Only one GPIO-to-bus-pin mapping pair should be selected for a given Core variant; the specification documents choosing one pair of jumpers, not shorting both alternative mappings together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R7\") (value \"0\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R15\") (value \"0\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"19\"))(node (ref \"R15\") (pin \"2\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"21\"))(node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"2\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R17\") (value \"0\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R24\") (value \"0\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The alternative M-BUS GPIO pins are tied together in pairs. This can short distinct Core signals together and make the selected PWM mapping unreliable or incompatible with the attached Core.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows zero-ohm links that enable mutually incompatible signal paths at once: the servo outputs are joined to each other and the transceiver path, and both alternative M-BUS GPIO mappings are shorted together. These connections conflict with the specification's assembly-time selection of mutually exclusive modes and mappings."
}

